            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph Reynolds",
                        "email": "joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "joseph-reynolds"
                    },
                    "message": "This looks good to me.  I happy to see progress in this area."
                },
                {
                    "file": "community-membership.md",
                    "line": 247,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph Reynolds",
                        "email": "joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "joseph-reynolds"
                    },
                    "message": "This point sounds like it addresses the project's infrastructure.  Whereas the next point addresses the ability of the security responder to reach technical experts needed to assess and resolve security vulnerabilities in the project's varied projects code bases.\nCan we add some words here to that effect?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "community-membership.md",
                    "line": 247,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I swapped one word infrastructure -> architecture, which is really what I intended.  The intent is that people on that team should understand OpenBMC enough to be able to gauge bugs, not just be able to pass off to other people.  Otherwise, we could just add all the subsystem maintainers to the security list and we wouldnt' need the extra role."
                },
                {
                    "file": "community-membership.md",
                    "line": 247,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "@joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com you +1ed this, so I'm assuming you're good here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "community-membership.md",
                    "line": 261,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph Reynolds",
                        "email": "joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "joseph-reynolds"
                    },
                    "message": "Note: When someone asks to join the openbmc-security email list and we reject their request, we can reference this point as the reason for the denial."
                },
                {
                    "file": "community-membership.md",
                    "line": 261,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "100% that is one of the things intended to quantify inclusion in the list.  I didn't add anything to that effect at this point, but we could in the future.  The real point is that the mailing list isn't a public mechanism for managing membership."
                },
                {
                    "file": "community-membership.md",
                    "line": 261,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "@joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com you +1ed this, so I'm assuming you're good here."
                },
                {
